acceptLoop's race can drop a just-accepted connection: 'race awaitClosing (N.accept lsock)' (bug-83 gate) kills the accept thread when the gate closes; if accept has already returned inside the doomed thread, the accepted fd is discarded -- the peer's connect() succeeded, so that client waits forever for a Welcome that never comes. Window only opens while a reload closes the gate, so it is rare and restart-family-only. Fix shape: accept under mask and hand the fd out via an MVar the gate path also drains, or replace race with a gate check between accept returns. | id:681413c5230bf66946bce3c524bc0240ccbc7b16
