BUG pane leaks when its shell exits behind a child that keeps the pty slave open (e.g. a backgrounded daemon like pomo that inherits stdout on the tty). The reader thread only tears the pane down on pty EOF, but a lingering fd-holder means the master never EOFs, so the pane persists in the tree with a dead shell -- unresponsive, un-exitable (exit/^C/^Z do nothing), and it pins the session and server alive. tmux keys pane death on the shell pid (SIGCHLD/waitpid), not pty EOF. Fix: wake the pane reader on shell-child exit (waitExit) and route through paneEof, so pane death tracks the shell -- remain-on-exit still honored. Found live: hf:11, pomo daemon held /dev/pts/47 fd 1/2. | id:e7d8dbde6e69c1052fde1dc6148d3b04593ef0ea
